{"title":"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3bee33a37450b329f86ab941005bed614fa872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2\\log{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/23408c965981962129a91822260679d4c2f6b199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\log{2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />. We may say that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcb0ece533b12d2c87f036ba7630de5cec9168c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{They do not intersect}\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{They intersect at 1 point only}\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{They intersect at 2 points only} \\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{They intersect at a finite number of points but greater than 2} \\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{They coincide}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"484\" height=\"96\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> into the other equation.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c7752d79d040b10dd338e894a96f60fa4525a359.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\log{x} = \\log{2x}\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" />\nUsing a logarithm property,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a641a1ad4f8ab424310a56b6f6b8b656bd5b6e28.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\log{x} = \\log{2} + \\log{x}\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" />\nSubtract both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb0c1e2d13ea3cd36f8938dab793c4c22b49f7e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/303a31d6e7e836b14094703bac06c19b55cfffc5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log{x}=\\log{2}\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.  Since both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/22761653f78b19cdd7ac2bf76fc091645f3ea72d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\log{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a3e349b086fb45102766d45fee18a3f899e826b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log{2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> are functions, there is only one corresponding y-value, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>By Ajeet Dubey | <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://ioqm.in\">ioqm.in</a></i>\n</p><p>A logarithm requires <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e28efa00c4f2c66d1aa381c0cb1f8e0ef8d6e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8ef22b9f5781d1d77e40102320af8dd000c90cc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\log x=\\log(x^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"21\" />, the equation becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab62599e4475476ffd1c6851e0ffd1a15cc2ad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(x^2)=\\log(2x).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" />\nSince the logarithm is one-to-one on positive numbers,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5bab9ae6faad28ab0a1dee25dc9e88bb7cde5774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=2x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" />\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8181ff295f638d646cacbbeda7c69e8e326afed2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x-2)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />. The value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is outside the domain, leaving only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore the two graphs meet at exactly one point.\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME\" title=\"1961 AHSME\">1961 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1961 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1961\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Pr